title crypto — Monocypher-source parity for the ChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD (RFC 8439 §2.8.2), GREEN
prompt take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; Rye prioritized; send often as its own signed round; approve your own design rounds; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur
think With Monocypher-source parity proven on BLAKE2b (hash), X25519 (key agreement), and Ed25519 (signing), the one remaining primitive family the decision wave named was the ChaCha/Poly line — and both the Ed25519 REMEMBER nib and its session log named it outright as the next durable crux, closing the four primitives against the actual audit target. That is Lindy-first crux-first: the fourth family completes the parity spine every module that seals or signs rests on.
think The tractable, highest-Lindy target on that line is the composed ChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD (crypto/aead.rye), not the two halves alone — one witness proves ChaCha20, Poly1305, and their RFC 8439 §2.8 binding at once. THE PARITY question was whether Monocypher exposes an IETF (RFC 8439, 12-byte nonce) AEAD matching ours, since crypto_aead_lock is XChaCha20 (24-byte nonce). It does: crypto_aead_init_ietf + crypto_aead_write. I read vendor/monocypher/src/monocypher.c to confirm the construction before trusting it — poly key from ChaCha20 djb counter (nonce_word<<32, low 32 bits 0), cipher at counter+1, MAC over ad ‖ pad16(ad) ‖ cipher ‖ pad16(cipher) ‖ le64(ad) ‖ le64(text) — byte-for-byte RFC 8439 §2.8, exactly what crypto/aead.rye composes.
think Reused the proven shape: a C harness linking the unmodified vendored Monocypher through zig cc, a Rye printing harness over the GREEN crypto/aead.rye (reached via three sibling symlinks in tools/ — aead, chacha20, poly1305). Chose RFC 8439 §2.8.2's own key/nonce/aad/plaintext (the sunscreen line) as the world anchor. Each harness prints two lines — ciphertext then tag — diffed byte-for-byte by the witness, both anchored to RFC 8439 §2.8.2's published ciphertext and tag so the oracle is a real second implementation.
obs GREEN on the first full pass: byte-identical ChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD across both the 114-byte ciphertext and the 16-byte tag, both matching RFC 8439 §2.8.2's published values (cipher d31a8d34…64b6116, tag 1ae10b59…0600691). Gate-free and purely local — the key and nonce are the RFC's public vectors, no key of ours, no signature, no network, no funds, no device. Count guard untouched (harness Rye in tools/, so crypto/*.rye stays 61); the monocypher parity witnesses stand outside the suite, as the three siblings do. Clean-room held — Monocypher linked, never copied.
obs The four primitive families the decision wave named — hashing (BLAKE2b), key agreement (X25519), signing (Ed25519), and authenticated encryption (ChaCha20-Poly1305) — now all meet the actual vendored Monocypher byte-for-byte. The Season G parity spine that the security audit rests on stands complete for the primitives; constant-time timing-safety remains the one named horizon across all four, wanting measurement rather than a claim.
loom witness=crypto_monocypher_aead_parity_witness result=GREEN values=2 impls=rye+monocypher_c anchor=rfc8439_2.8.2
file tools/crypto_monocypher_aead_parity_witness.rish the witness — builds the Monocypher IETF-AEAD harness, runs both, diffs byte-for-byte, anchors ciphertext and tag to RFC 8439 §2.8.2
file tools/fixtures/monocypher_aead_harness.c Monocypher's printing harness over the RFC vector via crypto_aead_init_ietf + crypto_aead_write, the IETF (RFC 8439) authenticated stream
file tools/monocypher_aead_parity.rye our authored printing harness over crypto/aead.rye's seal, the same inputs and two output lines
file tools/aead.rye symlink → ../crypto/aead.rye so the tools harness can import the GREEN composed AEAD
file tools/chacha20.rye symlink → ../crypto/chacha20.rye the stream-cipher half aead composes
file tools/poly1305.rye symlink → ../crypto/poly1305.rye the one-time authenticator half aead composes
file work-in-progress/REMEMBER.md Git nib head advanced to the ChaCha/Poly parity edge, Ed25519 demoted to prior edge
recommend keep-going — the four-primitive Monocypher-source parity spine is complete; next durable crux is a Comlink composition carrying a sealed Kumara message over the wire (a Claude check-in for the wire seam), or the docs-compression molt that feeds the seed; both are ungated and Lindy-high
